From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arseniy Velikanov <me@adomerle.pw>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:19:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: mediatek: Add MT6789 power domains

Add the MT6789 (Helio G99) SPM power domains: MD, CONN, MFG0-3, ISP,
IPE, VDEC, VENC, DISP, AUDIO, CAM and CAM_RAWA/B, with their bus
protection in infracfg. The IFR and DPY domains are left out: Linux must
never switch them.

Signed-off-by: Arseniy Velikanov <me@adomerle.pw>
[Patrick: from linux-mediatek mt6789-next a2a96be99f1b; read MD and CONN
 status from PWR_STATUS(_2ND) like the other domains; power MD with the
 modem sequence and external buck isolation, as MediaTek's LK does; keep
 ISP, IPE, AUDIO and the CAM domains off at probe, as the bootloader
 leaves them; checked against MediaTek's mtk-scpsys-mt6789.c]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
